{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.78,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_tolerance",
      "components": ["R35", "U5"],
      "pins": ["R35.1", "U5.27"],
      "nets": ["/BRB_{pH}", "GND"],
      "observed": "R35 is the 110 mΩ current-sense resistor for U5's BRB input, but its component fields specify a 20% tolerance. The other five matching current-sense resistors specify 1%. R35's listed part number, RL1220S-R11-F, and library-part description both indicate 1%, so the files are internally inconsistent.",
      "expected": "R35 should match the 1% tolerance used for the other TMC2209 current-sense resistors; at minimum, the BOM and part identity should consistently specify the intended tolerance.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"R35\") (value \"110mΩ\") ... (field (name \"PN\") \"RL1220S-R11-F\") ... (field (name \"Tolerance\") \"20%\") ... (field (name \"Description\") \"110 mOhms ±20% 0.333W, 1/3W Chip Resistor 0805\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"/BRB_{pH}\") ... (node (ref \"R35\") (pin \"1\")) (node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"27\") (pinfunction \"BRB\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(libpart ... (part \"RES 110mΩ ±1% 1/4W 0805 Susumu\") ... (field (name \"PN\") \"RL1220S-R11-F\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"R34\") (value \"110mΩ\") ... (field (name \"Tolerance\") \"\") ... (field (name \"Description\") \"110 mOhms ±1% 0.333W, 1/3W Chip Resistor 0805 (2012 Metric) Current Sense Thin Film\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If the 20% tolerance is used to source or populate R35, U5's phase-current setting can differ substantially from the intended setting, causing altered pump drive or current-limit behavior. The listed 1% part number makes an actual out-of-tolerance fitted part uncertain, but the design/BOM metadata discrepancy is clear.",
      "confidence": 0.78
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The files contain a clear tolerance inconsistency on R35, the pH pump driver's phase-current sense resistor. Its 20% tolerance field conflicts with the 1% part number and library description, and could affect current regulation if it reflects the fitted or sourced part."
}

